{
  "name": "The Bathroom Tile Installation Process: A Step-by-Step Guide",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting new tile in your bathroom is a fantastic way to refresh the space, but it's more than just sticking tiles to a wall! Here's a quick look at how the process usually goes down. Step 1: Inspection and Preparation. The installer will first check your existing surfaces to make sure they're sound, flat, and ready for tile. This might involve some leveling or repair – super important for a smooth finish. Step 2: Layout Planning. Before any tile goes down, a skilled installer will plan the layout to minimize cuts and make sure everything looks balanced. Step 3: Setting the Tile. Using the right mortar for your specific tile type, each tile is carefully set in place. Step 4: Grouting. Once the mortar has cured, grout is applied to fill the spaces between tiles. This is where color choice really comes into play! Step 5: Sealing. Finally, especially in wet areas, grout and sometimes the tile itself will be sealed to protect against moisture. Remember, this whole process often takes several days because there’s curing time needed between steps. If your project involves plumbing changes or waterproofing in showers, extra code review might be needed, depending on local rules. For a seamless tile installation in your Denver home, HH Remodeling has got you covered.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
